# LF in the working tree on every platform, not only inside the repository.
#
# Two reasons, both load-bearing. `packages/dshline/bin/dshline.mjs` is an
# executable with a shebang: checked out with CRLF, its first line ends in a
# carriage return and no Unix kernel will run it. And a CRLF copy of that same
# file cannot be imported through this project's test transform at all —
# "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" — which is how the Windows launcher
# job found this: Git for Windows converts to CRLF by default, so the focused
# launcher specs would not even load there.
* text=auto eol=lf
